<title>JAPAN: Sept Tokyo department store sales up 4.0 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Sept Tokyo department store sales up 4.0 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-10-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sales at Tokyo department stores in September rose 4.0 percent from a year earlier to 170.7 billion yen, the Japan Department Stores' Association said on Thursday.  </p>
<p>The year-on-year rise was largely due to active sales of autumn clothing, the association said.</p>
<p>Many department store operators renovated their outlets, which also gave a boost to their sales, it said.</p>
<p>The September data covered 29 outlets operated by 14 companies.</p>
</text>
